Ladybird reads the composition offsets of version 0 Composition Offset
(ctts) and Track Run (trun) boxes as signed.

Blink does the same: Chromium demuxes progressive MP4 with FFmpeg,
whose mov_read_ctts() reads every ctts offset into an int. And its MSE
parser’s TrackFragmentRun::Parse() reads trun offsets with Read4s(),
whatever the box version.

So does Gecko: Its mp4parse crate’s read_ctts() reads either version as
TimeOffsetVersion::Version1(be_i32(src)), citing buggy content that
writes negative version 0 offsets. And its MoofParser reads trun
offsets into an int32_t ctsOffset.

WebKit has no MP4 sample-table parser of its own to compare: WebCore
leaves demuxing MP4 to AVFoundation or GStreamer.
